Posted in RGRN and mailed to the Devteam.

On the current (or nearly current) DJGPP, the Makefile is broken.

The make I'm using reports version 3.79.1.  With the stock Makefile, the
dungeon compiler fails to parse dat/dungeon.pdf correctly, leading to a
broken build.

It turns out that the Makefile creates dgn_flex.c from dgn_comp.l as it's
supposed to, but instead of creating dgn_yacc.c, it grabs the one out of
sys/share.  The two don't match, and so the dungeon compiler is broken.

This doesn't affect the level compiler.

The problem turns out to be that there's no explicit rule to compile
dgn_yacc.o.  Make falls back on the implicit rules, and because the rule to
build from sys/share comes before the rule to build from util, the source
is drawn from sys/share.

Adding an explicit rule to build dgn_yacc.o fixes the problem:

--CUT HERE--CUT HERE--CUT HERE--CUT HERE--CUT HERE--CUT HERE--CUT HERE--
--- Makefile.GCC~       2003-12-07 18:39:14.000000000 +0000
+++ Makefile.GCC        2005-02-14 23:45:36.000000000 +0000
@@ -668,6 +668,18 @@
 $(U)dgn_comp.exe:  $(DGNCOMPOBJS)
        $(LINK) $(LFLAGS) -o$@ $(DGNCOMPOBJS)
 
+ifeq ($(YACC_LEX),Y)
+
+$(O)dgn_yacc.o:  $(HACK_H)      $(SP_LEV_H)    $(U)dgn_yacc.c
+       $(CC) $(cflags) -o$@ $(U)dgn_yacc.c
+
+else
+
+$(O)dgn_yacc.o:  $(HACK_H)      $(SP_LEV_H) $(INCL)/dgn_comp.h $(U)dgn_yacc.c
+       $(CC) $(cflags) -o$@ $(U)dgn_yacc.c
+
+endif
+
 ifeq  "$(DO_YACC)" "YACC_ACT"
 $(U)dgn_yacc.c $(INCL)/dgn_comp.h : $(U)dgn_comp.y
        @$(subst /,\,chdir $(UTIL))
--CUT HERE--CUT HERE--CUT HERE--CUT HERE--CUT HERE--CUT HERE--CUT HERE--

